# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-14); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: the most ordinary wish there is, on a MacBook Pro: Mail on the left, the chat on the right. 820 and 760 points and the gaps are
# 1628 of 1728, so both fit, whatever else is open: a Finder window floating somewhere is no reason for Mail to become a tile.
# Reference: T03 T20, F61.
display-size 1728x1117 33
open Mail 1100x700 min 820x500
open Slack 1100x750 min 760x500
open Finder 920x436 min 501x252
focus 101
key ctrl+opt+cmd+left
focus 102
key ctrl+opt+cmd+right
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
expect left-of 101 102
# A panel that opens later changes nothing either, now or at the next move of the view.
open Panel 300x200
zoom 102
show-all
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 104
# The chat closes: what was taken for it goes back, and Mail keeps no more than it had a right to.
close 102
expect visible 101
